In March 2023, several financial institutions ran into trouble: **Silicon Valley Bank in the U.S. collapsed and entered receivership, and Signature Bank was also shut down due to "systemic risk."** The crisis continued to spread - on March 19, Switzerland's largest bank, UBS Group, announced it would acquire the troubled Credit Suisse. **Amid this turbulent financial climate, how can you safeguard your assets?** On March 20, 2023, CCCWA - the China Chamber of Commerce of Washington State - held an in-person financial seminar, at which ICBC USA, a member of the Chamber's board of directors, analyzed recent major financial events and policies and explained its account service options. The seminar reviewed the collapse of Silicon Valley Bank, examining its underlying causes and its impact on the global economy. From the perspective of protecting the safety of your funds, it covered federal deposit insurance topics including coverage scope, insurance limits, and how to choose a bank. The seminar also introduced the features of ICBC USA's services: ICBC USA holds an S&P Global rating of A-, and its professional service team of 300 local employees provides bilingual Chinese-English service. Its current interest rates are competitive compared to major U.S. domestic banks, offering personal checking account customers an annualized rate of up to 3.5% and business checking accounts an annualized rate of up to 3.7%. The bank places strong emphasis on risk management to ensure the safety and stability of customer funds.

**ICBC USA currently offers a number of distinctive services**

- Fully waived fees on cross-border wire transfers to corporate accounts via the "China-U.S. ICBC Express Remittance" service;
- Convenient and efficient remote check deposit and small-value payment services through corporate account cash management;
- Personal credit cards available without an SSN, accepting domestic (Chinese) credit history, available on both VISA and UnionPay networks;
- Personal home loans available without an SSN, accepting domestic credit history, pay stubs, and financial assets;
- Loan-to-value ratio of up to 70%, with a maximum loan amount of $3.5 million;
- Student checking accounts suited to international students can be opened before arriving in the U.S., enabling direct remittances and tuition and fee payments...

